Build RDO's rpm-master python-django-horizon.spec without its documentation.

The spec turns documentation on by default, which drags in a Sphinx extension
EL10 does not package as an importable module:

    python3dist(sphinxcontrib-svg2pdfconverter) >= 0.1 is needed by
      python-django-horizon-1:25.7.3-1.el10.noarch

Only a `-common` subpackage of that exists on EL10, and it does not provide the
dist name the generated BuildRequires asks for. Horizon's documentation is not
part of what this shell deploys - the dashboard is - so the doc build is turned
off rather than a documentation toolchain being assembled to satisfy it. This
also drops the python-django-horizon-doc subpackage, which nothing here
installs.

Everything that actually serves the dashboard is unaffected: the spec's
%if 0%{?with_doc} blocks guard only the doc build and the doc package.

Second hunk: horizon 25.7.3 compiles 100 message catalogs in %build and its
pyproject wheel carries none of them, so the buildroot has empty locale trees
and the find-lang step fails with "No translations found for django". The
catalogs are copied into the two trees the install section lays out - the python
package under site-packages, and openstack_dashboard under
/usr/share/openstack-dashboard, which the spec has already moved by that point.

--- a/python-django-horizon.spec	2026-09-28 21:43:18
+++ b/python-django-horizon.spec	2026-09-29 06:56:24
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 %endif
 %global rhosp 0
 
-%global with_doc 1
+%global with_doc 0
 
 Name:       python-django-horizon
 # Liberty semver reset
@@ -259,6 +259,17 @@
 mv %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/openstack-dashboard/openstack_dashboard/conf/*.yaml %{buildroot}%{_sysconfdir}/openstack-dashboard
 mv %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/openstack-dashboard/openstack_dashboard/conf/nova_policy.d %{buildroot}%{_sysconfdir}/openstack-dashboard
 
+# horizon 25.7.3 compiles its message catalogs in the build section, but its
+# pyproject wheel does not carry them: 100 .mo files exist in the build tree and
+# none reaches the buildroot, so the lang-file step below finds nothing and the
+# build stops. Copy them into the two trees the install section has just laid
+# out. tar is used rather than a shell loop because a loop here ends up inside
+# the generated script and is easy to break.
+find horizon openstack_auth -name '*.mo' -print0 2>/dev/null \
+  | tar --null -cf - -T - | tar -xf - -C %{buildroot}%{python3_sitelib} || :
+find openstack_dashboard -name '*.mo' -print0 2>/dev/null \
+  | tar --null -cf - -T - | tar -xf - -C %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/openstack-dashboard || :
+
 %find_lang django --all-name
 
 grep "\/usr\/share\/openstack-dashboard" django.lang > dashboard.lang
